  data: {
    LLM: 'All cards are dealt out equally to the players; any remainder is stacked face up in the centre to start the play pile. Each player holds their cards as a face-down deck. Turn order is anti-clockwise, starting with the dealer. On your turn you reveal the top card of your deck and place it face up on the centre play pile. If your card matches the suit of the previous top card, you collect the entire play pile as your collected pile and get another turn immediately. If the suit does not match, your card stays on the pile and turn passes to the next player on your right. If your deck runs out you reshuffle your collected pile to form a new deck; if you have no collected pile you are eliminated. The last player left with all the cards wins.',
    Player: 'All cards are dealt out equally to the players; any remainder is stacked face up in the centre to start the play pile. Each player holds their cards as a face-down deck. Turn order is anti-clockwise, starting with the dealer. On your turn you reveal the top card of your deck and place it face up on the centre play pile. If your card matches the suit of the previous top card, you collect the entire play pile as your collected pile and get another turn immediately. If the suit does not match, your card stays on the pile and turn passes to the next player on your right. If your deck runs out you reshuffle your collected pile to form a new deck; if you have no collected pile you are eliminated. The last player left with all the cards wins.',
    objective: 'Collect all the cards in the deck through suit matching.',
    gameplay: 'All cards are dealt out equally to the players; any remainder is stacked face up in the centre to start the play pile. Each player holds their cards as a face-down deck. Turn order is anti-clockwise, starting with the dealer. On your turn you reveal the top card of your deck and place it face up on the centre play pile. If your card matches the suit of the previous top card, you collect the entire play pile as your collected pile and get another turn immediately. If the suit does not match, your card stays on the pile and turn passes to the next player on your right. If your deck runs out you reshuffle your collected pile to form a new deck; if you have no collected pile you are eliminated. The last player left with all the cards wins.',
    keyRules: [
      'Deal all cards equally; any remainder starts the centre play pile.',
      'Turn order is anti-clockwise from the dealer.',
      'On your turn reveal your top card and place it on the centre play pile.',
      "If your card matches the previous card's suit, take the whole play pile and take another turn.",
      'If it does not match, leave the card on the pile and pass turn to the player on your right.',
      'Reshuffle your collected pile when your deck is empty; no collected pile means elimination.',
      'Last player with all the cards wins.',
    ],
